th every distance along it the metric distance. On it $g_{rr} = r^6(r - 2m)^2/((r - m)^6Z)$ and the circle of radius $r$ has circumference $2\\pi r\\sqrt{Z}/(r - 2m)$.","At the strut, $r = 4\\,m$, a circle the distance $\\ell$ from the axis has circumference $\\tfrac{81}{64}\\cdot 2\\pi\\ell$, Emparan's excess of angle $(1 + m^2/b^2)^2$, so the tip is a cone in Minkowski space, $dX^2 + dY^2 - dZ^2$. Farther out the surface stands in flat space and widens as Flamm's paraboloid does; the same plane at every moment is the same surface."]}]}
